course: dictionary
lesson: 14331
title: Formal words: obtain
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Obtain is a formal word for get. You will meet it in exams, in science reports and in letters. When you read it, ask yourself: could I say get here instead? If the answer is yes, obtain means the same thing.
explain: «Mia had to obtain her mum's permission before she went to the park.» Permission means someone said yes. The word before it, had to, and the idea of asking tell you that obtain means to get something by asking.
explain: «The scientists obtained clear results from the experiment.» Results do not just appear. The scientists had to work for them, so obtain here means to get something through effort.
fact: Obtain means to get something, especially by effort or by asking.
fact: Obtain is a formal word. In everyday talk we usually say get.
fact: The past tense is obtained, and the -ing form is obtaining: «She is obtaining the books from the library.»
fact: Common phrases: obtain permission, obtain results, obtain a total.
fact: A rare, formal sense: rules that obtain are rules that exist or are in use.
exercise: «Mia had to obtain her mum's permission before she went out.» What does obtain mean here? | To hide a secret | *To get something by asking | To throw something away | To lose something
exercise: Which everyday word means about the same as obtain? | *get | sleep | throw | forget
exercise: «The scientists obtained clear results from the experiment.» What did the scientists obtain? | a broken tube | the scientists | *results | the experiment
test: «Sam obtained a total of 18 points in the quiz.» What does obtained mean? | copied | tidied | lost | *got
test: Which phrase uses obtain correctly? | obtain the sleepy dog | *obtain permission | eat obtain | sleep the permission
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to obtain? | *get | ignore | obey | forget
